rthritis, no recent joint pain or muscle aches.\n- **Neurological:** No headaches, no dizziness aside from reported episodes.\n\n**2. Objective:**\n\n**Physical Exam:**\n- **General:** Alert and oriented, appears in no distress.\n- **Neck:** Thyroid enlargement, non-tender.\n- **Cardiovascular:** Irregular heart rate and rhythm, no carotid bruits.\n- **Respiratory:** Clear to auscultation bilaterally.\n- **Abdomen:** Soft, non-tender, no hepatosplenomegaly.\n- **Extremities:** No edema in lower extremities.\n\n**Vital Signs:**\n- Blood Pressure: 130/85 mmHg\n- Heart Rate: 92 bpm, irregular\n- Respiratory Rate: 18 breaths per minute\n- Temperature: 98.6°F\n\n**Results:**\n- Blood Glucose: 250 mg/dL\n- Hemoglobin A1c: Elevated\n- Awaiting results for autoimmune panel including anti-GAD antibodies, anti-insulin antibodies, and thyroid function tests.\n\n**3. Assessment:**\n\n- **Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus with Hyperglycemia**\n  - **Medical Reasoning:** Patient has a new diagnosis of diabetes mellitus with elevated blood glucose levels and hemoglobin A1c. Given her family history of type 2 diabetes and her current lifestyle, this is most likely the diagnosis. However, autoimmune etiologies will be ruled out with pending lab results.\n- **Atrial Fibrillation**\n  - **Medical Reasoning:** Patient has a known history of atrial fibrillation, currently asymptomatic with no new concerns.\n- **GERD**\n  - **Medical Reasoning:** Patient is on protonix and reports compliance with the medication.\n\n**4. Plan:**\n\n- **Diabetes Management:**\n  - **Medical Treatment:** Initiate metformin 500 mg, oral, twice daily.\n  - **Additional Testing:** Complete metabolic panel, autoimmune panel including anti-GAD antibodies, anti-insulin antibodies, and thyroid function tests.\n  - **Patient Education and Counseling:** Educate the patient on the importance of blood sugar control, dietary modifications, and regular monitoring. Provide a glucometer and instructions on blood sugar testing.\n  