es joint pain or muscle aches. She does have osteoarthritis.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAMINATION\n\n• General: Appears in no distress.\n• Neck: Thyroid is slightly enlarged, but non-tender.\n• Cardiovascular: Irregular rate and rhythm.\n• Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.\n• Abdomen: Soft, no tenderness, no organomegaly, no hepatosplenomegaly.\n• Extremities: No edema.\n\nRESULTS\n\n• Blood glucose: Elevated.\n• Hemoglobin A1c: Elevated.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN\n\nHigh blood sugar.\n\n• Medical Reasoning: The patient presents with a history of high blood sugar. Her blood sugar and hemoglobin A1c are elevated. She has a history of atrial fibrillation and gastroesophageal reflux disease.\n\n• Medical Treatment: We will order a complete metabolic panel to evaluate for diabetes. We will start her on metformin 500 mg twice a day. We will hold off on insulin until we have the results of the autoimmune labs.\n\n• Patient Education and Counseling: The patient was advised to avoid foods high in sugar. The nurse will provide education on how to do blood sugar testing with the glucometer provided.\n\n• Referrals: None.\n\n• Additional Testing: We will order a complete metabolic panel.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nFollow up in 2 weeks to check blood sugar levels and to see if she needs insulin. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nHigh blood sugar.\n\nSOCIAL HISTORY\n\nThe patient reports that she is a social drinker and a non-smoker. She lives with her family and is currently in the midst of the holiday season. She states that she has been eating a lot of sweets during this time. She notes that she has been feeling dizzy and light-headed.\n\nMEDICATIONS\n\nMetoprolol 25 mg twice a day\nProtonix 40 mg once a day\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\n• Constitutional: Reports feeling dizzy and light-headed.\n• Cardiovascular: Denies chest pain or shortness of breath. Reports heart racing when anxious.\n• Gastrointestinal: Denies abdominal pain. Endorses history of reflux. Re