at her partner has been in sexual encounters with other people and she wants to be evaluated for all stds.\n\nThe patient reports that she has been experiencing some discharge, which is different in color and consistency than what she is used to. She also notes that the right side of her vagina has been sore and has not improved. She denies any fevers or chills.\n\nMs. Ross has a history of irregular pap smears in the past, but her last pap smear was normal 6 months ago.\n\nMEDICAL HISTORY\n\nMedical Reasoning\n\nMs. Ross is a 24-year-old female who presents today for full spectrum std testing. She reports symptoms of discomfort, a change in discharge, and odor in her vaginal region. She denies fevers or chills. She recently learned that her sexual partner has been in sexual encounters with other people, and she wants to be evaluated for all stds.\n\nThe patient\'s symptoms are concerning for stds, particularly chlamydia, gonorrhea, and trichomoniasis. The patient has a history of irregular pap smears in the past, but her last pap smear was normal 6 months ago.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\nExamination of the Genitourinary System\n\nPelvic exam demonstrates no external lesions. Normal labia majora and labia minora. Normal physiological discharge, with normal color and smell. Cervix is normal. Vaginal wall is normal. No cervical motion tenderness and no adnexal tenderness or masses noted. Swabs were done for std testing.\n\nRESULTS\n\nMs. Ross had std testing done today for gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, and blood was drawn for syphilis, hiv and hepatitis c. Some of these tests will take longer than others. We will call you if we see anything, but if you have not heard anything, you can call us in 3 days for results.\n\nASSESSMENT\n\nMs. Ross is positive for being high risk due to an abnormal pap smear in the past and the recent discovery of her sexual partner having multiple partners.\n\nPLAN\n\nThe patient was advised to return for follow up if she has any further sym