ee to evaluate the integrity of the ACL.\n  - Prescribe Meloxicam 50mg, oral, daily, to reduce pain and swelling.\n  - Advise patient to use ice as needed for pain and swelling.\n- **Lifestyle Modifications:**\n  - Moderate activities and avoid high-impact sports (soccer) until further evaluation and treatment.\n  - Use crutches for ambulation.\n  - Wear a knee immobilizer.\n  - Limit work activities and avoid prolonged sitting to reduce stress and strain on the knee.\n- **Follow-up:**\n  - Schedule follow-up in 1-2 weeks to review MRI results and reassess the patient\'s condition.\n\n**Patient Education:**\n- The patient understands the diagnosis and treatment plan. He is aware that further evaluation is needed to determine the extent of the ACL tear and that surgery may be necessary.\n- The patient is advised to follow the treatment plan and lifestyle modifications to reduce pain and swelling.\n\n**Patient Agreements:**\n- The patient agrees to follow the treatment plan and lifestyle modifications as advised.\n- The patient understands the potential risks and benefits of the treatment plan.\n\n**Patient\'s Agreement:**\n- The patient signs the informed consent form for the MRI and the treatment plan.\n- The patient understands the importance of adhering to the treatment plan and lifestyle modifications. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ PC: Scott, 28, male, SOHx: soccer player, presents with right knee injury 3 days ago. \nHx: sudden onset of pain while playing soccer, felt a pop in the knee, \nPain now 6/10, swelling has reduced, \nPMhx: none, \nSHx: no other medical problems, \nDHx: no relevant, \nPMhx: no relevant, \nFHx: no relevant, \nDHx: no relevant\nImp: Anterior Cruciate Ligament (ACL) tear, \nPlan: \n- MRI of the right knee\n- Meloxicam 50mg PO QD for 2 weeks\n- Ice application if necessary\n- Limit activities\n- Use crutches for ambulation\n- No jogging for the time being\n- Follow up with the doctor for the results of the MRI\n- Consider surgery based